# OAUTH-01 lane scope (issue #149): OAuth authorization, centralized refresh, credential health.
# Centralized fetch-and-discard token primitive (SEC-02 stays shut: no token
# persistence), auth-code/PKCE/callback contracts, audience/scope override
# semantics, non-secret health lifecycle. NinjaOne wired onto the primitive;
# halo auth shape unchanged.
# Persistence slice 1 (post-#148, migration 0031): encrypted per-org/per-Connection
# OAuth token + health rows reusing the ADR 005 envelope/KEK path, monotonic
# persisted generation with stale-generation fencing, no D1 tx over vendor HTTP.
# No callback/operator UI, no scheduled refresh, no new primitives, no
# integration-health aggregation.
